Subject: Lay out DB_PRIVATE regions like shared ones
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (Fil-C specific)

Private environments (DB_PRIVATE, and the implicit environment behind a
bare db_create(&db, NULL, 0) as used by cyrus-sasl's sasldb) use a heap
layout: every region allocation is a separate malloc, region "offsets"
(roff_t) are pointers cast to integers, mutex IDs are mutex addresses,
and shared queues link separately malloc'd objects with relative offsets.
Under Fil-C an integer cast back to a pointer has no capability, and an
offset from one object cannot reach another, so every private
environment trapped in __env_des_get (db_load, sasldb, ...).

Give private environments the layout that shared (mapped) regions use:
each region is one heap block of its maximum size, addressed by offsets
from its base, with index mutex IDs. ENV_HEAP_REGIONS() marks the checks
that select the heap layout; the other ENV_PRIVATE semantics (no files,
process-only mutexes, teardown on close) are unchanged.

ALIGNP_INC also round-tripped pointers through uintptr_t; add the
alignment padding to the pointer instead so it keeps its capability.

diff --git a/src/dbinc/db_int.in b/src/dbinc/db_int.in
index eae85c9..cba331d 100644
--- a/src/dbinc/db_int.in
+++ b/src/dbinc/db_int.in
@@ -187,7 +187,8 @@ typedef SH_TAILQ_HEAD(__hash_head) DB_HASHTAB;
 /* Increment a pointer to a specific boundary. */
 #undef	ALIGNP_INC
 #define	ALIGNP_INC(p, bound)						\
-	(void *)(((uintptr_t)(p) + (bound) - 1) & ~(((uintptr_t)(bound)) - 1))
+	(void *)((u_int8_t *)(p) +					\
+	    ((-(uintptr_t)(p)) & (((uintptr_t)(bound)) - 1)))
 
 /*
  * DB_ALIGN8 adjusts structure alignments to make sure shared structures have
